ook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMEI, NOBORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUNO, MITSUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMEI NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUNO MITSUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMEI, NOBORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUNO, MITSUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a polyester which comprises reacting a ketene with crotonaldehyde having a purity of 95 wt.% or higher. The unreacted crotonaldehyde remaining in the resultant reaction mixture may be recovered from the mixture and recycled to the reaction system. The crotonaldehyde to be fed to the system has an  alpha -vinylcrotonaldehyde content of, e.g., below 0.5 wt.%, and a paraldehyde content of, e.g., below 5 wt.%. The polyester obtained by the process is decomposed with, for example, hydrochloric acid to efficiently obtain sorbic acid having an excellent hue.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production de polyester, qui consiste à mettre en réaction un cétène avec un crotonaldéhyde ayant une pureté d'au moins 95 % en poids. Le crotonaldéhyde inaltéré restant dans le mélange réactionnel ainsi obtenu peut être récupéré dudit mélange et recyclé dans le système de réaction. Le crotonaldéhyde destiné à être alimenté dans le système présente une teneur en alpha-vinylcrotonaldéhyde inférieur, p. ex., 0,5 % en poids, et une teneur en paraldéhyde inférieur, p. ex., 5 % en poids. Le polyester obtenu par ce procédé est décomposé au moyen d'un acide chlorhydrique, par exemple, pour obtenir efficacement un acide sorbique présentant une excellente teinte.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>